 Pick the lean: binary-search the held lean whose projected arc stays on the road
 and ends nearest an asymptotic centre target.

 THIS IS THE HAZARD NOTES WARNS ABOUT. Twelve iterations, each deciding on a float
 comparison after simulating up to two thousand physics steps. A difference of 1e-7
 between f32 and f64 will eventually flip one of those comparisons, and from there
 the two rides are on different trajectories -- so a long trace comparison WILL go
 red and it will NOT mean the port is wrong. The check therefore compares ONE STEP
 FROM A SHARED STATE and never a trajectory.

 We say:

Section: Reading the Arc

  want-more-right : ArcOutcome, Real -> Boolean
  want-more-right (sim) (target) =
   when sim.shoulder
    is ShoulderLeft -> True
    is ShoulderRight -> False
    is ShoulderNone -> sim.end-across < target

Section: The Centre Target

 The target is an asymptote rather than the centre line: he aims at a fraction of
 his current offset, so he converges on the middle without ever committing to a
 lean that would overshoot it. Dead centre gets a signed epsilon instead, because
 a target of exactly zero has no side to lean toward.

  asymptote-tuning : Real
  asymptote-tuning = 0.30

  center-lane-epsilon : Real
  center-lane-epsilon = 0.04

  lean-target : Real -> Real
  lean-target (across) =
    if real-abs across < center-lane-epsilon then (if across >= 0.0 then center-lane-epsilon else 0.0 - center-lane-epsilon)
    else across * asymptote-tuning

Section: The Search

  max-tilt-correction : Real
  max-tilt-correction = 1.0 * deg

  lean-search-iters : Integer
  lean-search-iters = 12

  search-lean : RiderState, Segment, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Real
  search-lean (state) (seg) (target) (lo) (hi) (i) =
    if i >= lean-search-iters then (lo + hi) / 2.0
    else search-step state seg target lo hi i ((lo + hi) / 2.0)

  search-step : RiderState, Segment, Real, Real, Real, Integer, Real -> Real
  search-step (state) (seg) (target) (lo) (hi) (i) (mid) =
    if want-more-right (project-arc (with-tilt state mid) seg) target
      then search-lean state seg target mid hi (i + 1)
      else search-lean state seg target lo mid (i + 1)

  best-tilt-correction : RiderState, Segment -> Real
  best-tilt-correction (state) (seg) =
    search-lean state seg (lean-target state.across) (state.tilt - max-tilt-correction) (state.tilt + max-tilt-correction) 0
